cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these result tables, please cite the archived release below."
type: software
title: "scatac-aggregation-benchmark: code and result tables for a benchmark of aggregation scales for single-cell ATAC-seq gene activity"
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Chiu
    given-names: Yen-Jung
    affiliation: "Department of Biomedical Engineering, Chang Gung University, Taoyuan, Taiwan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/holiday01/scatac-aggregation-benchmark"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived result tables for a comparison of the scales on which
  single cells are aggregated into cell-type-level gene-activity profiles from
  single-cell ATAC-seq: raw, z-scaled and log-normalized means, pooled counts per
  million, the mean of counts per 10,000 and a coverage-matched control, evaluated
  on three cancer-associated datasets, 26 non-tumor tissues of a chromatin
  accessibility atlas and three matched RNA-ATAC datasets. No data files are stored;
  accessions and checksums are listed in data/.
keywords:
  - single-cell ATAC-seq
  - gene activity
  - normalization
  - aggregation
  - benchmark
  - marker genes
